      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "The improvement of regional and global ventricular function following percutaneous coronary intervention (PCI) with reperfusion of the artery supplying the infarct area in acute myocardial infarction is well-described. However, little is known of the potential effects of late recanalization of chronic coronary artery occlusion on left ventricular function."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "To determine whether PCI improves regional and global left ventricular function in patients with chronic coronary artery occlusions."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "PATIENTS AND METHODS",
          "content": "Thirty-five patients having at least one coronary artery occluded for six weeks or longer were included in the present prospective study. Exercise thallium-201 myocardial perfusion scintigraphy, multiple-gated acquisition ventriculography and two-dimensional echocardiography were performed in 19 patients (16 men; mean age of 58+/-5 years) who underwent a successful PCI to assess both regional and global left ventricular function before and six weeks following the procedure."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "The mean ejection fractions before and after reperfusion were 51+/-7% and 58+/-6% using Simpson's method (P<0.001) by echocardiography, and 45+/-1% and 53+/-1% (P=0.01) by multiple-gated acquisition ventriculography, respectively. The echocardiographic wall motion score was 24+/-9 before and 15+/-6 after PCI (P<0.001). The exercise perfusion score (21+/-1 and 14+/-1 [P=0.01]), rest perfusion score (15+/-1 and 12+/-1 [P=0.02]) and reinjection perfusion score (14+/-1 and 11.1+/-1 [P=0.07]) also improved after PCI. The presence of angina was strongly associated with an improvement in left ventricular function and wall motion score (P<0.01)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "PCI significantly improved the regional and global left ventricular function in patients with chronic total coronary occlusion. This procedure may provide symptom benefits in selected patients."
        }
      ]},
